# Line endings.
#
# Order matters: in .gitattributes the LAST matching pattern wins, so the
# generic normalisation rule comes first and the specific overrides follow.

# Everything is normalised to LF in the repository and checked out with the
# platform's native ending.
*      text=auto

# Binary assets must never be touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary

# start.bat is executed by cmd.exe, whose parser is byte-oriented: labels and
# `goto` targets are located by scanning for CR-terminated lines, and a
# LF-only batch file can fail to find a label or mis-parse a parenthesised
# block. The launcher relies on `goto :fail`, a `:scanargs` loop and several
# `if ... ( ... )` blocks, so CRLF is a correctness requirement, not cosmetics.
#
# `-text` rather than `text eol=crlf`: the latter normalises the blob to LF in
# the index and only converts on `git checkout`, so a GitHub "Download ZIP",
# `git archive`, or a raw-file fetch would still hand out LF-only bytes and
# reintroduce the problem for exactly the users least equipped to debug it.
# Disabling conversion stores the CRLF bytes verbatim, so every retrieval path
# produces a working file.
*.bat  -text
*.cmd  -text
